<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Castle, Delaware</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1651</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as New Amstel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Castle is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware River</a> in the US state of Delaware. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> founded it as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-casimir">Fort Casimir</a> in 1651, took it from the Swedes in 1655 and called it New Amstel; the English renamed it New Castle after 1664. It was the seat of the Lower Counties, the later colony of Delaware, until the capital moved to Dover in 1777.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-castle-delaware.jpg" alt="New Castle, Delaware" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ataraxy22 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Castle_Court_House_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
